# SlimPomo UI basics

Every new or changed UI element must meet these rules. Check them before finishing any task.

## Cursors
- Pointing hand (`NSCursor.pointingHand`) on every clickable custom control: buttons, icon buttons, mode gauges, count circles, ••• menus, push-back icons, disclosure chevrons, header icons (History, Tour, trash).
- I-beam on editable text. Open hand / closed hand for drag handles and while dragging.
- Disabled or display-only elements keep the arrow cursor.
- Standard `NSMenu` items and system controls keep their system cursors.

## Hover and states
- Every clickable custom control has a subtle hover state (e.g. a rounded background at white 6%, radius 6).
- Icon-only buttons: square 28×28 pt hit area with the icon centered. The hover/pressed background fills the square (radius 6). Round controls get a 28 pt circular hover. The icon size and the layout never change.
- Disabled: 40% opacity, no hover, a tooltip explaining why when that's useful.
- Hover must never shift the layout (no size or padding changes).

## Tooltips and accessibility
- Every icon-only control has a tooltip and an accessibility label.
- Custom controls expose the right accessibility role, and a hint when the click action isn't obvious.

## Layout
- The window is at least 450×550. Every element must fit there with nothing clipped.
- In rows, only the task name truncates (trailing "…"). Times, counts, and icons never truncate.
- Numbers and times use monospaced digits and fixed-width columns so rows line up.
- Keep existing spacing, font sizes, and colors. Reuse existing components instead of new styling.

## Row grid
- All list rows (Queue, LATER, Done, History) use the shared columns: Gauge (80 pt) · Name (flex, only this truncates) · Clock (60 pt, right-aligned) · Count (40 pt) · Action (28 pt square). The clock is 60 pt so a 12-hour time such as "12:50 AM" is not clipped.
- Same column = same meaning. Never place a different kind of value in a column.
- Count circles are controls. Display-only counts use plain text `×n`.
- Dividers: 1 pt, between rows only, starting at the Name column. No lines around section headers.

## Section headers
- Left-aligned, uppercase 11 pt medium label plus muted stats. Header icons sit in the Action column.
- Numbers use SF Pro with monospaced digits, never SF Mono.

## Motion
- Animations are short (150–300 ms) and play once. Never a second "catch-up" animation.
- Lists use stable ids. Reordering animates as a move, never remove + insert.
- Respect Reduce Motion: replace movement and scaling with a simple fade.

## Look
- Dark window, flat design. Use existing tokens and colors. No new colors without being asked.
- Sentence case for UI text. The menu bar follows standard macOS conventions.

## Before you finish
- [ ] Cursor, hover, and disabled states correct on every touched control
- [ ] Tooltip and accessibility label on icon-only controls
- [ ] Checked at 450×550 and at the default size
- [ ] Checked with Reduce Motion on
- [ ] No double animations or flicker
- [ ] Icon-only buttons have a 28×28 square hit area and hover
